IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `csrc-collection`

-- Child Support (Registration and Collection) Act 1988 (Cth) -- worked cases from the paying parent's seat.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case. The Child Support (Registration and Collection) Regulations 2018 are not deposited: the protected earnings rate
-- used below ($500 a week) and the general interest charge rates are ILLUSTRATIVE inputs, not the prescribed or published figures.
--
-- Fixtures are generated (scratchpad gen_child-support-registration-and-collection-act-1988_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Scenario facts used (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake/facts.json and SCENARIO.md): Jake, a security officer on
-- the award at Sentinel; separation in June 2038; a child support assessment by the formula for Ruby, payee Tahlia (k071,
-- 2038-06-15); "Three missed payments; the Registrar collects by deduction from his wages" (k072, 2039-01-15); a Part IX debt
-- agreement made in 2037 that completes on 2042-05-31 (k065, k075). Earlier he worked seven years for a delivery platform as an
-- "employee-like contractor". ASSUMED here, not in the scenario: Tahlia applied for the assessment and did not elect private
-- collection; Jake elected under s 44 to pay the Registrar himself and the Registrar accepted; a monthly liability of $780
-- ($180 a week); fortnightly pay of $2,100 after tax; three missed months making $2,340 of arrears.

§ `ss 17, 24A, 25 -- is my liability registered`

-- k071: Tahlia applied for the assessment and did not elect private collection, so the Registrar registers it at once.
#ASSERT `Is my liability registered` `a child support assessment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my liability registered` `a child support assessment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my liability registered` `a child support assessment` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my liability registered` `a child support assessment` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my liability registered` `a court order or court registered maintenance agreement` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 30, 38, 38A, 38B, 39 -- who collects`

#ASSERT `How is my child support collected` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `by the Registrar -- the amounts are debts I owe the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `How is my child support collected` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `privately -- my liability is not registered, so this Act does not collect it`
#ASSERT `How is my child support collected` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `privately -- my liability is registered but no longer enforced under this Act`

-- k072, on the other reading (private collection after a s 38A election): three missed payments mean Jake has not been
-- complying, so Tahlia's s 39 application must be granted, from a day no later than 60 days after it is received.
#ASSERT `Must the payee's application to collect again be granted` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Registrar must grant it`
#ASSERT `Must the payee's application to collect again be granted` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Registrar may refuse it`

#ASSERT `the latest day Registrar collection starts again` (Date 20 1 2039) EQUALS (Date 21 3 2039)

#ASSERT `What happens to my arrears when Registrar collection ends` `a s 38A election that includes the unpaid amounts` EQUALS `my arrears cease to be debts to the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT `What happens to my arrears when Registrar collection ends` `a s 38A election that does not include the unpaid amounts` EQUALS `my arrears stay debts to the Commonwealth and the Registrar can still collect them`

-- s 37B covers only s 17(1) liabilities (court orders and agreements); Jake's assessment is not covered.
#ASSERT NOT `May I apply for low-income non-enforcement` `a child support assessment` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I apply for low-income non-enforcement` `a court order or court registered maintenance agreement` TRUE FALSE

§ `Part IV -- collection from my pay`

-- k072: Jake at Sentinel is an employee; as a delivery contractor s 65AA would have reached him too.
#ASSERT `Am I an employee for Part IV` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an employee for Part IV` FALSE TRUE

-- k072: Jake's s 44 election had been accepted; he then missed three payments and the Registrar is not satisfied he will
-- resume, so the Register must be varied to say employer withholding applies (s 44(5)).
#ASSERT `Does employer withholding apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does employer withholding apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does employer withholding apply` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Does employer withholding apply` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does employer withholding apply` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `Must the Registrar collect from my pay` TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- k072: three months after withholding restarted Jake cannot opt out again; at seven months he may ask.
#ASSERT `May I elect that employer withholding not apply` TRUE 3 FALSE 0 EQUALS `not yet -- withholding restarted for missed payments less than 6 months ago`
#ASSERT `May I elect that employer withholding not apply` TRUE 7 FALSE 0 EQUALS `I may elect -- it takes effect if the Registrar is satisfied I am likely to pay on time`
#ASSERT `May I elect that employer withholding not apply` FALSE 0 TRUE 1 EQUALS `not yet -- my last election was rejected less than 2 months ago`

-- k072: $180 a week over a 14-day pay is $360. With $1,300 net the protected $1,000 caps it at $300; with $900, nothing.
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct from this pay` 180 14 2100 500 EQUALS 360
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct from this pay` 180 14 1300 500 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `How much can my employer deduct from this pay` 180 14 900 500 EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `By when must my employer remit my deduction` (Date 13 1 2039) EQUALS (Date 7 2 2039)
#ASSERT `By when must my employer remit my deduction` (Date 20 12 2039) EQUALS (Date 7 1 2040)

-- s 49: Jake is discharged by the deduction itself.
#ASSERT `How much do I still owe after the deduction` 2340 360 EQUALS 1980

#ASSERT `Does my employer commit an offence by acting against me` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my employer commit an offence by acting against me` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the most my employer can be fined under s 57, in penalty units` EQUALS 20

§ `Part V -- due dates and the late payment penalty`

-- k072: December 2038's amount (a calendar month) is due on 7 January 2039.
#ASSERT `When is my child support debt due` FALSE (Date 31 12 2038) EQUALS (Date 7 1 2039)
#ASSERT `When is my child support debt due` TRUE (Date 20 6 2038) EQUALS (Date 7 7 2038)

-- k072: $2,340 outstanding at an illustrative 11% a year: 2340 x 0.11 / 12 = $21.45 for the month.
#ASSERT `What late payment penalty for one period` `a calendar month` 2340 0.11 EQUALS 21.45
#ASSERT `What late payment penalty for one period` `a 4 week period` 1300 0.10 EQUALS 10

#ASSERT `May the Registrar remit my late payment penalty` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May the Registrar remit my late payment penalty` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May the Registrar remit my late payment penalty` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May the Registrar remit my late payment penalty` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `ss 71, 71C -- credits`

#ASSERT `How much of a direct payment must be credited` 500 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `How much of a direct payment must be credited` 500 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0

-- 30% of $780 is $234.
#ASSERT `How much of my prescribed payments must be credited` 780 300 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 234
#ASSERT `How much of my prescribed payments must be credited` 780 200 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `How much of my prescribed payments must be credited` 780 300 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of my prescribed payments must be credited` 780 300 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0

§ `ss 72, 72A, 72AA -- other sources`

#ASSERT `How much of my tax refund can be taken` 1200 2340 EQUALS 1200

#ASSERT `How much can a third person be made to pay` 5000 3000 2340 EQUALS 2340

#ASSERT `What can be deducted from my Centrelink payment` TRUE `a child support assessment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the prescribed periodic deduction may be taken`
#ASSERT `What can be deducted from my Centrelink payment` TRUE `a child support assessment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `only a lesser deduction may be taken -- financial hardship`
#ASSERT `What can be deducted from my Centrelink payment` FALSE `a child support assessment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no deduction under s 72AA`

§ `ss 72D-72L -- departure prohibition orders`

#ASSERT `Can a departure prohibition order be made against me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Can a departure prohibition order be made against me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `Must my departure prohibition order be revoked` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my departure prohibition order be revoked` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT `Must I be given a departure authorisation certificate` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I be given a departure authorisation certificate` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must I be given a departure authorisation certificate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by leaving Australia` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Do I commit an offence by leaving Australia` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `the most I can be fined for leaving, in penalty units` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the most I can be imprisoned for leaving, in months` EQUALS 12

§ `ss 30(3), 113A -- can the other parent sue me`

#ASSERT `Can the payee sue me` TRUE 14 FALSE EQUALS `yes -- by a s 113A proceeding, the Registrar having been told in time`
#ASSERT `Can the payee sue me` TRUE 7 FALSE EQUALS `not yet -- the payee must first give the Registrar 14 days' written notice`
#ASSERT `Can the payee sue me` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not limit it -- my liability is not registered`

§ `Debt agreements`

-- k072 with k065: Jake's debt agreement is in force in January 2039. On the Bankruptcy Act baseline's literal reading of
-- s 185K(3)(b) the deductions are forbidden there; this Act itself still requires them.
#ASSERT `Do my child support deductions continue during my debt agreement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `this Act still requires them, but the Bankruptcy Act bar read literally forbids them`
#ASSERT `Do my child support deductions continue during my debt agreement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `deductions continue -- this Act has no exception for a debt agreement`

